@ENTER SYSTEM,<SYSTEM-PASSWORD>,,<PROJECT>
@CC ===================================================================
@CC (UTILITY)DUMP-REENTRANT:MODE   --- GENERIC TEMPLATE ---
@CC Replace <SYSTEM-PASSWORD>/<PROJECT>. EDIT THE PRODUCT LIST to the
@CC subsystems this site actually has; delete the rest.
@CC
@CC Make the most-used ND-100 programs reentrant. Run once per COLD
@CC start (called from HENT-MODE:MODE). The reentrant segments live in
@CC the segment file and survive warm starts.
@CC
@CC Format: @DUMP-REENTRANT <name> <start-adr> <restart-adr> <file>
@CC   Start/restart addresses are OCTAL and come from each product's PD
@CC   sheet (they are the SAME on any machine). -1 = 177777, -3 = 177775.
@CC   Empty (,,) = use the file's own defaults.
@CC   File names use no directory prefix -> resolved on the default
@CC   directory. Add (<DIR>) only if a product lives elsewhere.
@CC ===================================================================
@CC
@CC --- SUBSYSTEM PACKAGE II (210400B): addresses VERIFIED vs PD sheet -
@DUMP-REENTRANT DITAP        70       70     (BPUN-FILES)DITAP-1880D:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT FMAC     177777   177775     (BPUN-FILES)FMAC:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT MAC      177777   177775     (BPUN-FILES)MAC-1415C:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT QED           0        1     (BPUN-FILES)QED:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT NPL           0        1     (BPUN-FILES)NPL-1896D:BPUN;1
@CC
@CC --- Other editors/tools: addresses PLAUSIBLE, VERIFY vs each PD sheet
@DUMP-REENTRANT PED           0        1     (SYSTEM)PED-ENG-J:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT NRL           0        1     (BPUN-FILES)NRL-1935I:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT GPM           0        1     (BPUN-FILES)GPM-2365B:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT FIL-EXTR      0        1     (BPUN-FILES)FIL-EXTR-2221B:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT BRF           0        1     (BPUN-FILES)BRF-EDITOR:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT LOOK-FILE     0        1     (BPUN-FILES)LOOK-FILE-2244D:BPUN;1
@DUMP-REENTRANT PERFORM-E     0        1     (BPUN-FILES)PERFORM-E:BPUN;1
@CC
@CC --- VERIFY these before trusting them ------------------------------
@CC FTN: confirm start/restart against the FORTRAN PD sheet.
@DUMP-REENTRANT FTN           0        1     (BPUN-FILES)FTN:BPUN;1
@CC ASSEMBLER-500: the manual dumps it with EMPTY addresses (,,), not 0/1.
@CC @DUMP-REENTRANT ASSEMBLER-500 ,, (BPUN-FILES)ASSEMBLER-500:BPUN;1
@CC ===================================================================
@CC END OF DUMP-REENTRANT:MODE
@CC ===================================================================
